chard-mille-watch-in-miami", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/sell-richard-mille-watch-in-miami/", "title": {"rendered": "Sell Richard Mille Watch in Miami"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4784, "slug": "online-shopping", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/online-shopping/", "title": {"rendered": "Shop at Home"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4701, "slug": "instagram-es", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/instagram-es/", "title": {"rendered": "Instagram SPA"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4698, "slug": "por-tren-brightline", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/por-tren-brightline/", "title": {"rendered": "Por Tren Brightline"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4696, "slug": "desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-palm-beach", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-palm-beach/", "title": {"rendered": "Desde el aeropuerto internacional de Palm Beach"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4694, "slug": "desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-fort-lauderdale", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-fort-lauderdale/", "title": {"rendered": "Desde el aeropuerto de Fort Lauderdale"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4692, "slug": "desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-miami", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/desde-el-aeropuerto-internacional-de-miami/", "title": {"rendered": "Desde el aeropuerto internacional de Miami"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4689, "slug": "contacto", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/contacto/", "title": {"rendered": "Contacto"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4687, "slug": "con-uber", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/con-uber/", "title": {"rendered": "Con Uber"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4684, "slug": "horario", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/horario/", "title": {"rendered": "Horarios"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4679, "slug": "como-llegar", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/como-llegar/", "title": {"rendered": "Como llegar"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4674, "slug": "servicios-de-seybold-building", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/servicios-de-seybold-building/", "title": {"rendered": "Servicios"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4673, "slug": "marcas", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/marcas/", "title": {"rendered": "Marcas"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4665, "slug": "servicios-de-joyeria", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/servicios-de-joyeria/", "title": {"rendered": "Servicios de joyer\u00eda"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4663, "slug": "destino-para-todo-tipo-de-producto-y-servicio-de-joyeria", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/destino-para-todo-tipo-de-producto-y-servicio-de-joyeria/", "title": {"rendered": "Destino para todo tipo de producto y servicio de joyer\u00eda"}, "content": {"rendered": "", "protected": false}}, {"id": 4660, "slug": "historia", "link": "https://seyboldjewelry.com/es/historia/", "title": {"rendered": "Historia"}, "content": {"rendered": "<p>Did John Seybold set out to be a jeweler? Of course not.</p>\n<p>But back at the dawn of the 20-th century when Miami was still largely terra incognito, John Seybold was a man with a vision.</p>\n<p>Armed with bread and confectionaries, he established his first business in Miami Avenue purveying baked goods to the neighborhood. Business was prolific, until a major fire burned down decades-worth of work and, soon, the baker would have to work his way up again, to save and build his business back from the ashes.</p>\n<p>The new premises were based in the buoyant Flagler road, where business was abuzz and the heartbeat of Miami was beating loud. Within a few years, John Seybold started expanding its business, buying and extending to nearby constructions.</p>\n<p>However, with the rapid development of the city, it soon became clear that the only way was up. The first three levels were constructed in 1921 by the nation renowned&nbsp;Kiehnel and Elliott architects. With a vast array of buildings registered under national heritage scheme, John Seybold was sure to work with the best in class to deliver his vision.&nbsp;This is how the Seybold Arcade was born; a landmark place filled with the latest fashions, offices, the best doctors in town and confectionaries of course!</p>\n<p>Within a few years, sever more stories were added to the main Arcade. The Seybold\u00ae <span style=\"font-size: inherit;\">Building was now a reality.</span></p>\n<p>But it wasn&#8217;t always a jewelry building. In the 1960s, the building\u2019s first jeweler moved in. Jeffrey Buchwald, a Hungarian immigrant who first opened his jewelry shop on the boardwalk in Atlantic City, moved to Miami to escape the cold. Then the Cuban Revolution brought a wave of jewelry artisans to the Seybold\u00ae, further establishing its footprint as a prime jewelry destination.</p>\n<p>Today, still located in the heart of downtown Miami, this 150,000 SF building is the third-largest diamond and jewelry center in the United States.&nbsp; A nationally registered historic landmark, the Seybold\u00ae building has a three-floor retail arcade with wholesale and manufacturing centers above, and houses over 300 jewelers.</p>\n<p>The world renowned Seybold\u00ae Building is recognized as a leader in the jewelry industry.</p>\n<div style=\"font-size: 12px;\">\n<p><em>Sources:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fusco Corporation</li>\n<li>Wikipedia</li>\n<li>The New Tropic</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p>\n\t\t\t<!-- START Over the years REVOLUTION SLIDER 6.6.20 --><p class=\"rs-p-wp-fix\"></p>\n\t\t\t<rs-module-wrap id=\"rev_slider_3_1_wrapper\" data-source=\"gallery\" style=\"vi